            <div xml:id="d904">

                <pb facs="1026" n="922" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg922"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.1051/729: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-12-24T14:00:00-05:45">December 24,
                            1932—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 25—12:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>247. Department’s telegram 132, December 22, 11 a.m. President Moncada has
                    submitted the basic law for the Guardia Nacional to Congress. The latter has
                    adjourned for the holidays and it is improbable that the project will be acted
                    upon until after the inauguration of Dr. Sacasa on January 1st.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
